# HLF (the Lever N hang shapes and the skewed eight with the 8 s decode-gap floor, on the TRAFFIC profile the image bakes in, ONE fresh boot): the decoder finishes, all decoders finish, a cancel mid-prefill,
# an arrival during a prefill, the seed stops, the eight steady, the drain and the skew. This tests the floor fix (HL-LN v584 and v620 failed the same shapes with a 199 s and a 207 s decode-less stretch).
# READ: the container log has '[PINDIAG] lever N governor: ttft=180 gap_floor=8'; levern_alternation_problems is clean (no decode-less stretch above the floor plus one prefill step, about 16 s);
# concurrent8_skew: the slowest first token is under 238 s and the shorts keep their round; every user at budget, no refusal, no hang (no host block in execute_trace, no watchdog dump), no garbage or empty stream,
# no program compiled after the warm. Soft class: a failure is data and never strands the hand-back.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Lever N decode-gap floor window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags
# and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-12b is the window image (built from tp4/levern-alternation-fix: the Lever N traffic profile with the 8 s decode-gap floor baked in as its default).
# C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. No profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-12b
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,levern_decoder_finishes,levern_all_decoders_finish,levern_cancel_mid_prefill,levern_arrival_during_prefill,levern_seed_stops,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_skew
C2_BOX_MINUTES=55
